US English speaker learning Brazilian Portuguese, A1, ordering at a restaurant. Brazilian words and forms ("o cardápio", "a conta", "Eu quero...", "Por favor"), not European Portuguese ("a ementa"). Tips should target sounds English speakers get wrong (nasal "ão", the "r" in "carro" sounding like "h", open and closed vowels). Respellings use English spelling habits ("kar-DAH-pee-oo").